# .dockerignore
# Everything not excluded here is uploaded to the daemon and can land in an
# image layer. Layers are readable by anyone who can pull the image, so the
# build context must never carry credentials, VCS history, local caches or
# host-built artefacts. See chapters 22, 23 and 24.
#
# Patterns are relative to the context root (not gitignore semantics), so
# anything that can appear at any depth is written with a leading **/.

# --- VCS and CI metadata ---
.git
.gitattributes
.gitmodules
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml
.circleci
**/.gitignore

# --- Credentials and key material (must never reach a layer) ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/id_ecdsa*
**/*.ppk
**/secrets
**/.netrc
**/.pypirc
**/credentials
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/.terraform
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.template
!**/env.template

# --- Docker and compose files (the build itself does not need them) ---
**/Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile.*
**/*.dockerfile
**/.dockerignore
**/docker-compose*.yml
**/docker-compose*.yaml
**/compose*.yml
**/compose*.yaml

# --- Editor and OS noise ---
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~

# --- Local state, logs and archives ---
**/tmp
**/temp
**/*.log
**/*.tar
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.tgz
**/*.zip

# --- Package manager auth files ---
**/.npmrc

# --- Documentation (checked: no COPY in this context depends on it) ---
**/*.md
**/docs

# --- Go ---
bin/
**/vendor
**/*.test
**/*.out

# Host-built binary sitting next to the sources; `COPY . .` would
# otherwise push a stale macOS executable into a Linux image.
/bet-builder
